It is five minutes to six.
I open the door.
In the shop it is warm and dark.
There are sacks of coffee everywhere.
A man stands behind the counter.
"Good evening," I say.
"Good evening," answers the man.
I ask him: "Which coffee do you recommend?"
He shows me two kinds.
"You must smell this one," he says.
I smell the coffee.
The smell is wonderful.
I choose the dark coffee.
"I'll take this one," I say.
He weighs the beans and I pay.
He gives me the packet and the receipt.
I put everything into my backpack.
Then I go back outside.
The sun shines on the water.
I walk a little further along the river.
